### Usage Instructions ###
# 1. First run the Sign Up request to create a new user
# 2. Then run the Sign In request to get the authentication token
# 3. Copy the token from the signin response
# 4. Replace {{auth_token}} in the subsequent requests with your actual token
# 5. Now you can test all the book endpoints with authentication

# Note: The token is valid for 24 hours after signing in
# Make sure your MongoDB server is running and the JWT_SECRET is set in your .env file

### Email Notification Testing ###
# To test email notifications:
# 1. Update the .env file with your actual email credentials:
#    - EMAIL_USER=your-email@gmail.com
#    - EMAIL_PASS=your-app-password (for Gmail, use App Password, not regular password)
#    - ADMIN_EMAIL=recipient@example.com
# 2. Run the "Add New Book" requests above
# 3. Check the server console for email status messages
# 4. Check the recipient email inbox for notifications
# 5. If emails fail, check the console for error messages

# Gmail App Password Setup:
# 1. Enable 2-Factor Authentication on your Gmail account
# 2. Go to Google Account settings > Security > App passwords
# 3. Generate a new app password for "Mail"
# 4. Use this app password in EMAIL_PASS (not your regular Gmail password)
